---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Tile from "../components/Tile.astro";
---
<Base title="about — velocit.ee" description="Why velocitee exists, who it's for, and how we actually intend to keep the lights on.">
  <section>
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-wrap px-6 lg:px-10 py-16">
      <p class="label">// about</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 font-mono text-4xl md:text-5xl text-cream tracking-tightest leading-[1.05] max-w-[26ch]">
        for the orgs whose IT is held together by one person who'll move on next year.
      </h1>
      <div class="mt-8 grid lg:grid-cols-[1.1fr,1fr] gap-12">
        <div class="prose">
          <p>
            velocitee exists because the small organisations that need solid infrastructure the most are also
            the ones that can least afford to maintain it. School STEM labs. Community nonprofits. Local
            sports clubs. The infrastructure inevitably ends up being run by one volunteer who knows where
            the bodies are buried — and when they leave, everything starts to crumble.
          </p>
          <p>
            The existing tools assume an audience that doesn't match. Enterprise platforms assume a budget.
            Open-source tooling assumes a sysadmin. Cloud SaaS assumes you're fine sending student data to
            another continent. None of them are wrong; they just aren't aimed at us.
          </p>
          <p>
            So we're building velocitee — an open-core deployment platform that takes hardware from bare
            metal to a documented, running stack, with a single config file as the source of truth.
            Open source under AGPL v3, self-hostable forever. The paid SaaS layer is for people who want
            extra hands; the engines themselves are free.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>The full pipeline is four engines</strong> — VME (metal), VNE (network), VSE (services),
            VLE (lifecycle). We're shipping them in order. VME shipped first. VNE shipped next. We'll keep
            shipping until the pipeline is done, and we'll keep documenting the whole thing as we go.
          </p>
        </div>

        <aside class="space-y-5">
          <Tile title="founder" status="ok">
            <p class="text-cream font-mono text-base font-semibold">Finley Karras</p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-muted text-2xs font-mono">student engineer · IT admin · germany</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-muted text-sm font-sans leading-relaxed">
              Runs the IT infrastructure for a school STEM lab. Currently studying engineering. Builds and
              maintains the entire velocitee stack — server, engines, docs, this website — out of a basement
              in Germany.
            </p>
          </Tile>
          <Tile title="who works on this" status="ok">
            <p class="text-muted text-sm font-sans leading-relaxed">
              One person, full-time-ish, plus contributors who've sent PRs. The community is small but the
              engines are stable. You can <a href="https://github.com/velocit-ee" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-green-hi underline-offset-2 hover:underline">read all our code</a>.
            </p>
          </Tile>
          <Tile title="where it runs" status="ok">
            <p class="text-muted text-sm font-sans leading-relaxed">
              Production velocit.ee runs on a Proxmox VM behind Cloudflare Tunnel — same kind of setup
              the engines themselves provision. We use our own tools.
            </p>
          </Tile>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-y border-border bg-surface/30">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-wrap px-6 lg:px-10 py-16">
      <p class="label">// principles in practice</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 font-mono text-3xl text-cream tracking-tightest leading-[1.1]">how we make decisions.</h2>
      <ul class="mt-9 grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-2">
        <Tile title="01" status="ok">
          <h3 class="text-cream font-mono text-base font-semibold tracking-tightest">Correctness above all.</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-muted text-sm font-sans leading-relaxed">
            We'd rather ship one engine that works correctly than four engines that maybe work. Verification
            is a hard gate — the engines refuse to write a manifest if checks fail.
          </p>
        </Tile>
        <Tile title="02" status="ok">
          <h3 class="text-cream font-mono text-base font-semibold tracking-tightest">Lightweight.</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-muted text-sm font-sans leading-relaxed">
            Every layer of indirection earns its keep. Where we can ship a single Python module, we ship
            a single Python module. The engines aren't there to be impressive — they're there to disappear.
          </p>
        </Tile>
        <Tile title="03" status="ok">
          <h3 class="text-cream font-mono text-base font-semibold tracking-tightest">Provisioner-agnostic.</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-muted text-sm font-sans leading-relaxed">
            We don't pick favourites. Use OpenTofu, use Ansible, use our native Python runner, use Pulumi
            (when someone writes that renderer). The schema doesn't change.
          </p>
        </Tile>
        <Tile title="04" status="ok">
          <h3 class="text-cream font-mono text-base font-semibold tracking-tightest">Open core, AGPL forever.</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-muted text-sm font-sans leading-relaxed">
            We will never relicense the engines from AGPL to anything more restrictive. If the company
            disappears tomorrow, the engines are still yours, still maintained by you and the community.
          </p>
        </Tile>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-wrap px-6 lg:px-10 py-16">
      <p class="label">// roadmap</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 font-mono text-3xl text-cream tracking-tightest leading-[1.1]">where we are. where we're going.</h2>
      <ol class="mt-10 relative">
        <li class="flex gap-6 pb-10 relative before:absolute before:left-[14px] before:top-7 before:bottom-0 before:w-px before:bg-gradient-to-b before:from-green before:to-border">
          <span class="bg-green text-bg w-7 h-7 inline-flex items-center justify-center text-2xs font-semibold shrink-0">01</span>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-cream font-mono text-base font-semibold tracking-tightest">VME — metal · live</h3>
            <p class="mt-1 text-muted text-sm font-sans leading-relaxed max-w-[58ch]">
              PXE boot any x86_64 hardware, install Proxmox VE or Ubuntu Server fully unattended.
              Foundation everything else builds on. Stable.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-6 pb-10 relative before:absolute before:left-[14px] before:top-7 before:bottom-0 before:w-px before:bg-gradient-to-b before:from-green before:to-border">
          <span class="bg-green text-bg w-7 h-7 inline-flex items-center justify-center text-2xs font-semibold shrink-0">02</span>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-cream font-mono text-base font-semibold tracking-tightest">VNE — network · live (initial)</h3>
            <p class="mt-1 text-muted text-sm font-sans leading-relaxed max-w-[58ch]">
              OPNsense VM, VLANs, DHCP, DNS, firewall. Two backends ready, eleven reserved.
              Iterating to "active" stability over the next release cycle.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-6 pb-10 relative before:absolute before:left-[14px] before:top-7 before:bottom-0 before:w-px before:bg-gradient-to-b before:from-warn before:to-border">
          <span class="bg-warn/80 text-bg w-7 h-7 inline-flex items-center justify-center text-2xs font-semibold shrink-0">03</span>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-cream font-mono text-base font-semibold tracking-tightest">VSE — services · next</h3>
            <p class="mt-1 text-muted text-sm font-sans leading-relaxed max-w-[58ch]">
              Containerised stacks on top of VNE’s network. Design phase. Alpha targets common nonprofit
              workloads (Nextcloud + LDAP + monitoring as a starter bundle).
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-6 relative">
          <span class="border border-border bg-surface text-muted w-7 h-7 inline-flex items-center justify-center text-2xs font-semibold shrink-0">04</span>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-cream font-mono text-base font-semibold tracking-tightest">VLE — lifecycle · planned</h3>
            <p class="mt-1 text-muted text-sm font-sans leading-relaxed max-w-[58ch]">
              Drift detection, auto-docs, single-command repair. Furthest out — design crystallises after
              VSE has enough mileage to know what actually drifts.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
